And so on for all the comments you'd like to convert to `Assert` statements.

It's important to note that `some_position_of_x_in_the_same_array` is going to be a placeholder and should be replaced with the appropriate conditions or values involved in the comment. For instance, if the comment said "the last position of x in old array is greater than a specific position", then you would search for that position and replace it before converting to the equivalent `Assert` line.--------------------```cs
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= New_arrListIndexOfX);
```

This assertion checks that the last position of x in the old array is greater than or equal to the first position of x in the new array after removal. This indicates that the array maintains its order of elements even after performing the remove operation.--------------------Here is the list of output assert statements corresponding to the comments that start with "@@@":

```cs
